## Alcohol (ethanol)
component-ethanol = Alcohol (ethanol)
    .genitive = alcohol
component-ethanol-description-novice = A colourless liquid that boils already at 78 °C and freezes only at −114 °C — no home freezer can freeze it.
component-ethanol-description-school = Ethanol has about 40 % lower specific heat than water and a 2.6 times lower heat of vaporisation. So it heats up and boils away much faster.
component-ethanol-safety-school = Alcohol catches fire easily and its vapour can explode. Real alcohol is never heated over an open flame.
